## Write

Creates or overwrites a file at the specified path with the given content.

Usage:
- Prefer Edit over Write for modifying existing files — Edit is faster and uses less bandwidth
- Only use Write to create new files or when you need to completely replace a file's content
- Never use this tool to edit an existing file — use Edit instead
- When creating a parent directory for a new file, prefer to create the file directly with its full path; Write will create intermediate directories automatically.
- When writing a file, you must include ALL of the contents of the file, even if you haven't changed them. Partial writes are not allowed.
- For Jupyter notebooks (.ipynb files), always use the Write tool (never Edit). The content must be valid JSON conforming to the nbformat spec.
- Always prefer writing files in the current working directory or project directories that clearly belong to the user

